  reported_speech:
    interference_patterns:
    - pattern: No backshift of tenses in reported speech
      example: She said that she is tired.
      frequency: 4
      persistence: 4
      communicative_impact: 3
      example_l1: Dia bilang bahwa dia capek
      example_gloss: She say that she tired
      example_wrong: She said that she is tired.
      example_correct: She said that she was tired.
      explanation: M/I reported speech retains the original tense. English requires backshift (present -> past, will -> would).
      etiology: interlingual
      flagged: false
      tier: 3
    - pattern: Direct speech patterns in reported speech
      example: He told me he will come tomorrow.
      frequency: 3
      persistence: 3
      communicative_impact: 2
      example_l1: Dia bilang saya akan datang besok
      example_gloss: He say I will come tomorrow
      example_wrong: He told me he will come tomorrow.
      example_correct: He told me he would come the next day.
      explanation: M/I does not change time references or pronouns in reported speech the way English does.
      etiology: interlingual
      flagged: false
      tier: 3
    examples:
    - wrong: She said that she is tired.
      correct: She said that she was tired.
    - wrong: He told me he will come tomorrow.
      correct: He told me he would come the next day.
    why_it_happens: M/I reported speech retains the original tense. English requires backshift of tenses and changes to time/place references. (Swan & Smith, p. 289)
    teacher_tips:
      how_to_explain: 'Teach the backshift rule: present -> past, will -> would, tomorrow -> the next day. M/I keeps the original tense; English changes it.'
      where_to_start: Start with tense backshift. Then teach time/place reference changes.
      sequencing: 'Week 1: Tense backshift. Week 2: Time/place reference changes. Week 3: Question reporting. Week 4: Review.'
      exercises:
      - name: reported_speech Audit
        type: error-correction
        description: 20 sentences with reported speech errors from M/I learner writing.
        duration: 15
      - name: reported_speech Translation
        type: translation
        description: Translate 15 sentences focusing on reported speech.
        duration: 15
      - name: reported_speech Practice
        type: fill-in-the-blank
        description: 20 sentences practicing reported speech.
        duration: 10
      - name: reported_speech Error Hunt
        type: error-correction
        description: A paragraph with 10 reported speech errors.
        duration: 15
    sources:
    - Swan & Smith Learner English (Indonesian)
    - Parrott Grammar for English Language Teachers
    source_count: 2
