  linking_words:
    interference_patterns:
    - pattern: Conjunction duplication (although...but)
      example: Education although expensive but is valuable.
      frequency: 4
      persistence: 4
      communicative_impact: 3
      example_l1: Pendidikan meskipun mahal tetapi berharga untuk masa depan
      example_gloss: Education although expensive but valuable for future
      example_wrong: Education although expensive but is valuable for a good future.
      example_correct: Although education is expensive, it is valuable for a good future.
      explanation: Conjunctions and linking expressions may be duplicated. M/I commonly uses paired conjunctions (meskipun...tetapi) where English uses only one.
      etiology: interlingual
      flagged: false
      tier: 3
    - pattern: Conjunction duplication (as a result because)
      example: I failed my exam as a result because I didn't study hard.
      frequency: 3
      persistence: 3
      communicative_impact: 2
      example_l1: Saya gagal ujian sebabnya karena saya tidak belajar
      example_gloss: I failed exam because-of-it because I not study
      example_wrong: I failed my exam as a result because I didn't study hard.
      example_correct: I failed my exam as a result of not studying hard. / I failed my exam because I didn't study hard.
      explanation: Linking expressions may be duplicated. M/I allows multiple causal connectors where English uses one.
      etiology: interlingual
      flagged: false
      tier: 3
    - pattern: Unbalanced structures with 'and' and 'or'
      example: I like to watching TV and read the story book.
      frequency: 3
      persistence: 3
      communicative_impact: 2
      example_l1: Saya suka menonton TV dan membaca buku cerita
      example_gloss: I like watch TV and read book story
      example_wrong: When I have time I like to watching TV and read the story book.
      example_correct: When I have time I like watching TV and reading story books.
      explanation: Structures with and and or may be unbalanced. M/I does not require parallel structure as strictly as English.
      etiology: interlingual
      flagged: false
      tier: 3
    examples:
    - wrong: Education although expensive but is valuable for a good future.
      correct: Although education is expensive, it is valuable for a good future.
    - wrong: I failed my exam as a result because I didn't study hard.
      correct: I failed my exam because I didn't study hard.
    - wrong: When I have time I like to watching TV and read the story book.
      correct: When I have time I like watching TV and reading story books.
    - wrong: I was late for school and suddenly I got up and with quick I brush my teeth.
      correct: I was late for school and suddenly I got up and quickly brushed my teeth.
    why_it_happens: M/I writers tend to avoid complex sentences. When learners use them, they may not structure them well. Conjunctions and linking expressions may be duplicated (meskipun...tetapi). (Swan & Smith, pp. 289-290)
    teacher_tips:
      how_to_explain: 'Teach: In English, use ONE conjunction per clause. Although (NOT although...but). Because (NOT because...as a result). Keep parallel structure with and/or.'
      where_to_start: Start with conjunction duplication errors (although...but, because...as a result). Then teach parallel structure.
      sequencing: 'Week 1: Conjunction duplication. Week 2: Parallel structure. Week 3: Complex sentence structure. Week 4: Review.'
      exercises:
      - name: linking_words Audit
        type: error-correction
        description: 20 sentences with linking words errors from M/I learner writing.
        duration: 15
      - name: linking_words Translation
        type: translation
        description: Translate 15 sentences focusing on linking words.
        duration: 15
      - name: linking_words Practice
        type: fill-in-the-blank
        description: 20 sentences practicing linking words.
        duration: 10
      - name: linking_words Error Hunt
        type: error-correction
        description: A paragraph with 10 linking words errors.
        duration: 15
    sources:
    - Swan & Smith Learner English (Indonesian)
    - Parrott Grammar for English Language Teachers
