  gender:
    interference_patterns:
    - pattern: Gender pronoun confusion (dia = he/she/it)
      example: She cannot believe got five distinction.
      frequency: 3
      persistence: 3
      communicative_impact: 2
      example_l1: Dia tidak percaya dapat lima distinction
      example_gloss: He/She not believe get five distinction
      example_wrong: John sat for exam and passed. She cannot believe got five distinction. Her parents very happy.
      explanation: Gender is not expressed grammatically in M/I. One word, dia (he/she/it), is used for third-person singular subject, object and sometimes possessive pronouns.
      etiology: interlingual
      flagged: false
      tier: 2
    examples:
    - wrong: She cannot believe got five distinction.
      correct: He cannot believe he got five distinctions.
    - wrong: Her parents very happy.
      correct: His parents are very happy.
    why_it_happens: Gender is not expressed grammatically in M/I. One word, dia (he/she/it), is used for third-person singular subject, object and sometimes possessive pronouns. (Swan & Smith, p. 283)
    teacher_tips:
      how_to_explain: 'Teach: English distinguishes he/she/it. M/I uses dia for all. Pay attention to the gender of the person being referred to.'
      where_to_start: Start with he vs she. Then teach possessive pronouns (his/her/its). Then practice with context.
      sequencing: 'Week 1: he/she/it. Week 2: his/her/its. Week 3: Practice with context. Week 4: Review.'
      exercises:
      - name: gender Audit
        type: error-correction
        description: 20 sentences with gender errors from M/I learner writing.
        duration: 15
      - name: gender Translation
        type: translation
        description: Translate 15 sentences focusing on gender.
        duration: 15
      - name: gender Practice
        type: fill-in-the-blank
        description: 20 sentences practicing gender.
        duration: 10
      - name: gender Error Hunt
        type: error-correction
        description: A paragraph with 10 gender errors.
        duration: 15
    sources:
    - Swan & Smith Learner English (Indonesian)
    - Parrott Grammar for English Language Teachers
    source_count: 2
    source_type: textbook
